+### Skin finish
+
+Optional `skinFinish: 'reduced-sheen'` requests quieter highlights from the skin's second specular
+lobe. Omit it or use `'original'` to retain the existing material defaults. Other values, including
+null and numeric weights, are rejected before GPU setup. The choice is fixed at creation and follows
+figure rebuilds; create another Avatar to change it.
+
+Reduced sheen changes only the second-lobe weight from 0.34 to 0.12. Its roughness remains 0.24, and
+the skin maps, regional roughness and remaining material settings retain their existing behavior.
+`report().skin` reports the requested finish, whether the skin material is attached to the current
+body, its active `clearcoat`/`clearcoatRoughness`, and construction settings. Missing or disposed
+skin reports null material fields and `attached: false`. Reduced sheen makes
+`report().scene.lighting.calibrated` false because it is outside the historical material calibration.
+
+This is an opt-in artist choice. The retained Neutral Studio portrait comparison supports a modest
+quieter sheen with readable face volume; it does not qualify preference across lighting, bodies or
+motion. It is not yet part of Showcase settings or saved-look JSON; their exporter refuses this
+finish rather than silently saving it as Original.
+
 ### Hair colour
 
 With a hair style enabled, optional `hairColour: '#765344'` supplies a six-digit sRGB material colour. Uppercase hex is accepted and normalized to lowercase. Named CSS colours, shorthand hex, numeric values, null and colour without a hair style are rejected. Omit the option to retain the exact existing derived default; a rounded hex is not substituted for that default.
